+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers currently cannot get a discount after placing an order. The checkout flow
+needs to accept a coupon on a pending order, reduce the amount due, and record the
+redemption atomically so totals and usage limits stay consistent.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": string }`.
+- Validate the request, order, and coupon according to a fixed precedence of error codes.
+- Compute the discount (FIXED or PERCENT, optional cap, never below zero) and return the
+  updated order with the same shape as `GET /orders/:id`.
+- Persist the order update, a `coupon_redemptions` row, and the coupon usage increment in a
+  single transaction; any failure leaves the database unchanged.
+- Reject re-use on an order that already has a coupon, including the same coupon twice.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `order-coupons`: applying a coupon code to a pending order, covering discount computation,
+  validation/precedence, atomic redemption recording, and the resulting order representation.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+<!-- None: no existing spec covers order coupon application. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts`: register the new route and parse the request body.
+- `src/services/orderService.ts`: add the application rule and orchestration.
+- `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts`: persist discount fields.
+- `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts`: read/increment usage and insert redemptions.
+- `src/app.ts`: wire the coupon repository into `OrderService`.
+- New tests under `tests/` built on the in-process `app.request(...)` harness.
+- No schema, dependency, or existing-test changes; `npm run build` and `npm test` must pass.
