+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository support
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, { discountCents, finalAmountCents, couponCode, now })` that, inside a single transaction, updates the order row, increments `coupons.used_count` for the normalized code, and inserts a `coupon_redemptions` row, rolling back and rethrowing on any error. Verify with `npm run build`.
+- [x] 1.2 Confirm `CouponRepository.findByCode` exposes `usedCount`, `usageLimit`, `validFrom`, `validUntil`, and `status` needed by the service, adding no new SQL unless a field is missing. Verify with `npm run build`.
+
+## 2. Service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Inject `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` and wire it in `app.ts`. Verify `npm run build`.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` performing checks in error-precedence order: input validation, order lookup, pending status, no existing coupon, coupon lookup, ACTIVE, `validFrom <= now < validUntil` via the injected `Clock`, usage limit, and minimum amount. Verify each rejection with a focused test.
+- [x] 2.3 Compute the discount (FIXED, PERCENT floor, optional cap, clamp to amount) and call `OrderRepository.applyCoupon`, returning the reloaded order. Verify AC-01 through AC-06 with tests.
+
+## 3. Route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, parsing the id and passing `couponCode` through, returning HTTP 200 with the order. Verify with an end-to-end `app.request` test.
+
+## 4. Tests
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add tests covering every acceptance criterion (AC-01..AC-10) and every error code, using a fixed `Clock`. Verify with `npm test`.
+- [x] 4.2 Add a test asserting rejected requests leave the order, coupon `usedCount`, and `coupon_redemptions` unchanged. Verify with `npm test`.
+
+## 5. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 5.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and confirm both pass without modifying existing tests or the schema.
